                                          2290  #-----------------------------------------------------------------------
                                          2291  #
                                          2292  #  vCPU extension functions (for acceleration and compaction) follow below.
                                          2293  #
                                          2294  #  The naming convention is: SYS_<CamelCase>[_v<V>]_<N>
                                          2295  #
                                          2296  #  With <N> the maximum number of cycles the function will run
                                          2297  #  (counted from NEXT to NEXT). This is the same number that must
                                          2298  #  be passed to the 'SYS' vCPU instruction as operand, and it will
                                          2299  #  appear in the GCL code upon use.
                                          2300  #
                                          2301  #  If a SYS extension got introduced after ROM v1, the version number of
                                          2302  #  introduction is included in the name. This helps the programmer to be
                                          2303  #  reminded to verify the acutal ROM version and fail gracefully on older
                                          2304  #  ROMs than required. See also Docs/GT1-files.txt on using [romType].
                                          2305  #
                                          2306  #-----------------------------------------------------------------------
                                          2307
